{
  "pedal": "Boss PH-3 Phase Shifter — focused reamp, every mode (mono)",
  "comment": "Two kinds of take. Tones: nine quiet sines together (113 Hz to 8.9 kHz), nothing else — a phaser is a filter that moves, and each tone's level and phase on the output is that filter at its frequency at every moment, all through the sweep, at any Rate (October read it from noise folded on the cycle). Guitar: excerpts of captures/di/ at -12 dB over an 8 kHz probe (the model against the pedal on real playing: waveform, bands; the probe places the model's sweep on the pedal's). Per Stage mode: the phaser standing still (Depth 7:00; a sweep), then sweeping at full Depth with Res off and fully up. 4 Stage also at Depth 12:00 (full-level funk twice: the pedal against itself; the lead held out) and at three more Rates. Rise, Fall and Step last. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; 9:00 and 3:00 pointer horizontal. Takes ordered so each step turns one or two knobs.",
  "quiet_dbfs": -60,
  "knobs": [
    "Mode",
    "Rate",
    "Depth",
    "Res"
  ],
